< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/looper/issues/116#issuecomment-6819401630 Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/cluster#18
Issue #116 is fixed and committed, but not landed yet: no build runner will take the build, so the manager can't give a verdict. I've marked the issue `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/cluster#18` and left it open.

- **Fix:** commit 285b910 on `looper/looper-116`, rebased on main f81cca4. It is the same change as the earlier 2a2906c. Each Actions run now keeps its `head_branch`, and a failed run counts as recovered only when a later run of the same workflow succeeds on the same ref. When something is still broken, the summary names those refs, e.g. "4 of 5 runs failed; still red: v2.1.13, v2.5.15, v2.6.3".
- **Tests:** the new scenario `actions-recovered-on-the-same-ref` in `tests/looper-recap.test.sh` checks three cases:
  - failed tags followed by a success on a different tag stay red;
  - a later success on the same tag recovers it;
  - a success *before* the failure on the same tag recovers nothing.

  I ran the suite here and it ends `looper-recap: all scenarios pass`.
- **Why the last land failed:** it wasn't a test failure. The manager's build waited 3h with its status stuck at "pending" and gave no verdict. My own build of 285b910 (gate set `recap`) still had no status after 30 minutes, which #113 treats as no runner taking it.
- **Land:** queued again with the manager at 09:03Z. If a runner takes its build and it passes, the manager merges it, and the next run posts the outcome comment and closes the issue.
- **Why it's blocked:** #113 is stuck on the same thing, cluster#18 (the build pool). Starting more builds here would only add load to that pool.

I posted the status on the issue; the trace rule doesn't apply, since no service handler was touched.
